course: dictionary
lesson: 2825
title: Diverse: many kinds together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Diverse means made up of many different kinds of people or things, or very different from each other. Look at the words around it for clues. In a diverse class, the children come from many backgrounds, so the class is a mix.
explain: «Canada welcomes immigrants from all over the world and calls itself a mosaic of cultures, and Toronto is one of the most diverse cities on Earth.» The clues are all over the world and a mosaic of cultures. A mosaic is made of many different pieces, so diverse must mean full of many different kinds of people.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: «Toronto is one of the most varied cities on Earth» still makes sense, so you are right. The noun is diversity, which means the mix of differences in a group or place.
fact: Diverse means made up of many different kinds of people or things, or very different from each other.
fact: «Diverse» can describe a place, a group, a range of things, or a habitat.
fact: «A diverse range of» means a wide variety of different things.
fact: In science, a rainforest is a diverse habitat with many species; this is called «biodiversity».
fact: The noun is diversity, and «culturally diverse» means having people from many different cultures.
exercise: «Toronto is one of the most diverse cities on Earth.» What does diverse mean here? | Lost and hard to find | *Made up of many different kinds of people | Very small and quiet | Ancient and very old
exercise: «The rainforest is a diverse habitat with many species.» What does diverse suggest? | *Many different kinds of plants and animals | Only one kind of tree | Empty and silent | Very cold and dry
exercise: Which word is the noun form of diverse? | *diversity | diverse | diverge | divert
test: «The school offers a diverse range of clubs.» What does diverse range mean? | A short list of rules | Only one club to choose | *A wide variety of different clubs | Clubs that are closed
test: Which phrase describes a country with people from many backgrounds and cultures? | Culturally late | *Culturally diverse | Culturally empty | Culturally quiet
exam: Zara says «a diverse class» means a class where everyone wears the same uniform. Is she right? | Yes, because diverse means identical | No, diverse means very old | Yes, everyone in a diverse class is the same | *No, diverse means made up of many different kinds of people
